<figure class="field-guide reckoning-visual">
  <header>
    <p>Application map</p>
    <h3>One local slope, three different questions</h3>
  </header>
  <div class="panels">
    <section>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="motion-title motion-desc">
        <title id="motion-title">Position and instantaneous velocity</title>
        <desc id="motion-desc">A rising position curve with a tangent line whose slope gives velocity.</desc>
        <path class="axes" d="M28 15v110h192" />
        <path class="curve blue" d="M30 119C77 117 89 101 115 75s45-49 100-55" />
        <path class="line lime" d="M73 119l103-97" />
        <circle class="dot lime-fill" cx="121" cy="68" r="4" />
        <text x="31" y="143">time, t</text>
        <text x="38" y="22">position, s(t)</text>
      </svg>
      <h4>Motion</h4>
      <p>The slope of position is instantaneous velocity.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="cost-title cost-desc">
        <title id="cost-title">Cost and marginal cost</title>
        <desc id="cost-desc">A cost curve with a tangent line whose slope gives the cost of producing a little more.</desc>
        <path class="axes" d="M28 15v110h192" />
        <path class="curve pink" d="M30 118C78 114 109 99 137 72s48-43 78-48" />
        <path class="line lime" d="M88 119l107-92" />
        <circle class="dot lime-fill" cx="139" cy="70" r="4" />
        <text x="31" y="143">quantity, q</text>
        <text x="38" y="22">cost, C(q)</text>
      </svg>
      <h4>Economics</h4>
      <p>The slope of total cost is marginal cost.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 240 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="loss-title loss-desc">
        <title id="loss-title">Loss and a gradient descent step</title>
        <desc id="loss-desc">A bowl-shaped loss curve with an arrow pointing downhill toward lower loss.</desc>
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto">
            <path d="M0 0l8 4-8 4z" class="pink-fill" />
          </marker>
        </defs>
        <path class="axes" d="M28 15v110h192" />
        <path class="curve blue" d="M34 28C67 95 86 113 122 113s55-22 92-87" />
        <circle class="dot lime-fill" cx="184" cy="67" r="4" />
        <path class="descent" d="M179 73l-40 28" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)" />
        <text x="31" y="143">model weight, w</text>
        <text x="38" y="22">loss, L(w)</text>
      </svg>
      <h4>Machine learning</h4>
      <p>The slope identifies a direction that reduces loss.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>What to notice:</strong> each field gives the axes different names. The mathematical
    operation remains a measurement of how quickly the vertical quantity changes near one input.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

